            <field name="code">C05</field>
            <field name="name">Card programming</field>
            <field name="evidence_level">documented</field>
            <field name="publication">public_scoped</field>
            <field name="allowed_copy">Supported SmartphoneKey reader configurations also let you program MIFARE Classic and MIFARE DESFire EV3 cards. Technical answer (FAQ, MIFARE guide, compatibility page only): Cards are programmed with a SmartphoneKey reader that supports programming; SmartphoneKey does not support third-party card programmers.</field>
            <field name="limitations">Owner-stated clarification 2026-10-27 (not a new hardware test): SmartphoneKey does not support third-party card-programming devices; programming is an additional capability of supported SmartphoneKey reader configurations. Never imply an external or extra programmer, never lead the home page, the reader proposition or short summaries with it, and do not make the absence of third-party support a headline. Not every reader configuration; no EV1/EV2, memory-size, other-family or credential-format inference. Reading, programming, assigning access and using a card are separate operations.</field>
            <field name="internal_source">P05, P06, P07, owner-stated clarification 2026-10-27</field>
